Dear fellow LaTeX Gurus,

I'm sending this message on behalf of our glorious leader (Frank) who
had to spend the beginning of the week in bed and is still a bit sick.

Frank and I recently discussed the question of how we are going to test
the things we are developing.  The first thing must (of course) be a
thorough testing at our local installations.  But then we need to give
it away to some beta testers.  We see two (major) possibilities for this:
 - build a new LaTeX system with the improvements included
 - distribute a lot a files that implement the different features.
    This means that we must rip LaTeX apart.
Comments and suggestions are welcome.

And now it is time for me to wish you a very happy Easter (also in the
name of Frank).  Have a nice weekend and don't start working hard too
early again!

   Rainer


